ttached to a specific note, the direction element","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"can be associated with the first note element that follows it in score order that is not in a different voice.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection"},"doc://IvorMXL/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP","title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSound":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsound","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSound"}],"title":"MXLSound","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSound","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSound"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The sound element contains general playback parameters. They can stand alone within a part\/measure, or be a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component element within a direction."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/SQ":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","title":"Swift.Equatable","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If a barline is other than a normal single barline, it should be represented by a barline type that describes"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"it. This includes information about repeats and multiple endings, as well as line style. Barline data is on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same level as the other musical data in a score — a child of a measure in a partwise score, or a part in a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"timewise score. This allows for barlines within measures, as in dotted barlines that subdivide measures in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"complex meters. The two fermata elements allow for fermatas 